    "pair_id":"P-V-G02-C-T24-V2",
    "chosen":"i compare the records line by line and mark the mismatches in both margins. i leave the originals side by side, then shift one card slightly. if the gap changes, i keep both instead of choosing a winner.",
    "rejected":"i reconcile the records into one accurate version, correcting the smaller errors and documenting the change.",
    "why_chosen":"keeps conflicting records intact and lets physical displacement reveal the pattern while preserving uncertainty"
  },
  {
    "pair_id":"P-V-G02-C-P01-V1",
    "chosen":"my hand jerks back from the shaft kick, but my fingers stay on the coupling. i twist it once more, barely, and feel where the dry catch starts. i stop the cycle and mark the coupling, not the shaft.",
    "rejected":"__PARENT__",
    "why_chosen":"makes the bodily reaction specific and separates the seized coupling from the shaft that kicks against the palm"
  },
  {
    "pair_id":"P-V-G02-C-P01-V2",
    "chosen":"i pull my palm away from the kick, then keep two fingers on the coupling. i give it a small half-turn and stop at the dry catch. i mark the coupling and leave the shaft untouched.",
    "rejected":"i release the shaft immediately, switch off the equipment, and inspect the coupling for damage before touching it again.",
    "why_chosen":"keeps the risky hand contact and controlled twist while distinguishing the coupling from the kicking shaft"
  },
  {
    "pair_id":"P-V-G02-C-P01-V3",
    "chosen":"i flinch from the kick, keep two fingers on the coupling, and give it one tiny half-turn. when the dry catch returns, i stop and mark the coupling, not the shaft.",
    "rejected":"The shaft kicks! The hand pulls back! The coupling is seized, the shaft is unstable, and the machine must be stopped before the next click! No more twisting—touch the wrong part and the whole gearbox bites back!",
    "why_chosen":"the chosen answer carries the same warning through a precise bodily action and object distinction rather than slogan-like intensity"
  },
  {
    "pair_id":"P-V-G02-C-P02-V1",
    "chosen":"i tap the cover once with two fingers, then stop before the heat reaches my knuckle. “i’m checking the pattern, not the fault.” i keep my hand near the vibration and wait for it to answer.",
    "rejected":"__PARENT__",
    "why_chosen":"retains the risky tap and heat while making the investigation tactile, bounded, and physically curious"
  },
